        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugène Ionesco, Paul Scott\n- Roles: playwright, novelist, poet\n- Concepts: French Avant-garde theatre, The Raj Quartet\n\nFacts:\n- Eugène Ionesco was born as Eugen Ionescu on 26 November 1909.\n- Paul Scott was born as Paul Mark Scott on 25 March 1920.\n- Eugène Ionesco was a Romanian-French playwright who wrote mostly in French.\n- Eugène Ionesco was one of the foremost figures of French Avant-garde theatre.\n- Paul Scott was an English novelist, playwright, and poet.\n- Paul Scott was best known for the tetralogy The Raj Quartet.\n- Paul Scott died on 1 March 1978.\n- Eugène Ionesco died on 28 March 1994.",
